secubox-sentinelle-gsm (0.4.0-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * FM RDS surface — new lib/sentinelle_gsm/rds_runner.py wraps a
    rtl_fm | redsea pipeline at 171 kHz to decode the 57 kHz RDS
    subcarrier (PI, PS, RT, TP, TA, PTY, AF). Mirrors LivemonRunner's
    spawn/watch/stop lifecycle so the api/main.py device-claim layer
    refuses concurrent GSM + FM scans on the same RTL-SDR.

  * lib/sentinelle_gsm/rds_observations.py: RdsStationRegistry stores
    one row per Programme Identification code in the shared
    observations.db (table rds_stations). UPSERT keeps the latest PS
    and RT while preserving the previous values when a bare-PI frame
    arrives (COALESCE on each field).

  * lib/sentinelle_gsm/rds_sweep_job.py: async-job model for a
    /rds/sweep that walks the FM band (default 87.5 -> 108.0 MHz in
    200 kHz steps x 10 s dwell, ~17 min total). Same JobRegistry +
    state machine as scan_auto_job v0.3.6 — operator POSTs and polls
    GET /rds/sweep/jobs/{id} for progress without blocking the HTTP
    thread.

  * api/main.py: new POST /rds/start, POST /rds/stop, GET /rds/status,
    GET /rds/stations, POST /rds/sweep, GET /rds/sweep/jobs[/{id}],
    POST /rds/sweep/jobs/{id}/cancel. Device-busy detection unified
    via _device_busy_reason() so both GSM and RDS endpoints return a
    consistent 409 with the conflicting subsystem named.

  * debian/rules ships the redsea binary at /usr/libexec/secubox/
    secubox-redsea (built natively on arm64 with -O2, no LTO, single
    job; cross-build refused to link liquid-dsp's NEON intrinsics).
    The runner picks up the path via SECUBOX_REDSEA_BIN env var with
    that hardcoded default.

  * www/sentinelle: new RDS panel with manual-tune controls (freq,
    gain, ppm), sweep launcher with live progress bar, and a table of
    observed stations sortable by last_seen / count / PI.

  * L3 decoder (lib/sentinelle_gsm/l3_decode.py): now walks the first
    4 bytes of the GSMTAP raw_l3 payload looking for the protocol-
    discriminator byte instead of assuming the L3 message starts at
    offset 0. BCCH/CCCH downlink frames carry a L2 pseudo-length prefix
    and SDCCH uplink frames carry a short LAPDm header; both used to
    leave parse() returning ParsedFrame() with no decode. This was
    why MCC/MNC/LAC/CI stayed null on every sighting. New parsers
    cover MM Identity Response (0x19), MM Location Update Request
    (0x08), and RR Paging Response (0x27) — gives us TMSI/IMSI
    extraction from uplink SDCCH on top of the existing Paging Request
    downlink. _decode_mcc_mnc() now refuses MCC < 200 (no valid ITU
    country code) so a misaligned frame can no longer poison the DB
    with bogus '0-0-0-CCCC' cell_id entries. 8 unit tests added
    against real Orange France hex (MCC=208 MNC=01 LAC=0x2901).

  * scanner.py: cast ppm to int before invoking grgsm_scanner; the
    binary refuses '60.0' with 'invalid integer value' and aborted
    every scan-auto job on a board with a non-integer ppm value.

  * menu.d/45-sentinelle.json: menu id renamed sentinelle → sentinelle
    -gsm so the hub's _check_module_active() probe finds secubox-
    sentinelle-gsm.service (was looking for secubox-sentinelle); URL
    path stays /sentinelle/ for back-compat. debian/rules ships a
    sentinelle-gsm → sentinelle symlink under /usr/share/secubox/www/
    so the install probe also passes.

